%description:

TcpCubic.hystartEnabled:on -- HyStart ends slow start without a loss.

The claim (TcpCubic.ned): "HyStart: leave slow start when the path appears full, instead of
overshooting into loss".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true, the value of LinuxTcp and LegacyTcp). The code: HyStart acts in slow start when the window is at least hystartLowWindow segments
(TcpCubic::processRttSample()). TcpCubic::hystartUpdate() looks for the exit: detector 1, the
ACK train, and detector 2, the delay increase, whose threshold is the minimum RTT / 8, clamped
to hystartDelayMin and hystartDelayMax (TcpCubic::hystartDelayThresh()). At the exit, ssthresh
becomes the window. TcpCubic::initializeAlgorithm() checks the values. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic, which sends to host2; the path is host1 -- tap -- router -- host2, with a bottleneck of 10 Mbps from the router to
host2 and a round trip of 40 ms. host2 has a window of 1000000 bytes and acknowledges each
second segment (the delayed ACK), so its ACKs come 2.4 ms apart, more than the ACK delta of 2
ms: they form no ACK train, and only the queue at the bottleneck can end slow start. Observation: level 3, at 1.2
s, HyStart found the exit, and the threshold is the window at the exit, at most 300000 bytes
(about 210000).

%# parameter: TcpCubic.hystartEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.hystartEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpCubicHystartEnabledOn")
        .act(action().at(1.2)
                 .describe("the state at 1.2 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.hystart_found == true && state.ssthresh <= 300000"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicHystartEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.hystartEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.linkDelay = 5ms
*.bottleneckDatarate = 10Mbps
*.bottleneckDelay = 10ms
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 1000000
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 10000000B
sim-time-limit = 1.3s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpCubicHystartEnabledOn: PASS
